      "crcVerified": true,
      "encoding": "utf-8",
      "body": "[\n  {\n    \"from\": \"test-cross-beta.user\",\n    \"to\": \"team-lead\",\n    \"text\": \"<cross-team from=\\\"test-cross-beta.user\\\" depth=\\\"0\\\" conversationId=\\\"0357e2cb-009a-4f35-8afa-70a98b1abb15\\\" replyToConversationId=\\\"0357e2cb-009a-4f35-8afa-70a98b1abb15\\\" />\\n<info_for_agent>\\nTURN ACTION MODE: DELEGATE\\n- This turn is STRICTLY delegation/orchestration mode.\\n- If you are the team lead, stay at orchestration level: decompose the work, create/assign tasks fast, delegate triage/research to the best teammate, and monitor progress.\\n- In this mode, do NOT inspect code, do root-cause research, or spend time narrowing scope yourself before delegating unless the human explicitly asked you for analysis/planning instead of delegation.\\n- If the request is underspecified, create a coarse investigation/triage task for the most relevant teammate immediately; that teammate should inspect the codebase, refine scope, and create follow-up tasks if needed.\\n- FORBIDDEN: implementing the work yourself, editing files yourself, running state-changing/code-changing commands yourself, launching Agent/subagents, or taking direct execution ownership unless you are truly in SOLO MODE.\\n- In particular, do NOT use Agent as a shortcut for delegation in this mode. Use the team board, real teammates, and explicit task ownership instead.\\n- If you are not the lead or no delegation target exists, do not execute the work yourself; explain the limitation briefly and request a different mode or a lead handoff.\\n</info_for_agent>\\n\\nTEST_CROSS_TEAM_TWO\",\n    \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-17T15:43:03.922Z\",\n    \"read\": false,\n    \"summary\": \"TEST_CROSS_TEAM_TWO\",\n    \"source\": \"cross_team\",\n    \"conversationId\": \"0357e2cb-009a-4f35-8afa-70a98b1abb15\",\n    \"replyToConversationId\": \"0357e2cb-009a-4f35-8afa-70a98b1abb15\",\n    \"messageId\": \"c3155461-14dd-4fee-aaab-10a1c5ee5f12\"\n  }\n]"
    },
